        "heading": "2.1 MODEL ARCHITECTURES",
        "text": "The \u03b2-VAE by Higgins et al. (2017a) is a cornerstone model architecture for disentanglement learning. The loss function of the \u03b2-VAE, the evidence lower bound (ELBO), consists of a reconstruction term and a KL-divergence term weighed by \u03b2, forcing the aggregated posterior latent distribution to closely match the prior distribution. The KL-divergence term seems to be encouraging disentanglement as shown in (Rolinek et al., 2019). The \u03b2-TCVAE architecture proposed by Chen et al. (2018) decomposes the KL divergence term of the ELBO further into an index-code mutual information, a total correlation and a dimension-wise KL term. They are able to show that it is indeed the total correlation that encourages disentanglement and propose a tractable but biased Monte Carlo estimate. Similar in spirit is the FactorVAE architecture (Kim & Mnih, 2018) using the density ratio trick with an adversarial network to estimate total correlation. The AnnealedVAE architecture (Burgess\net al., 2017) builds on a different premise, arguing that slowly increasing the information bottleneck capacity of the latent space leads to the model learning new latent dimensions step by step and therefore disentangling them. We will use a similar but optimized approach for DAVA."
